WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.347
Intervals can also shift time.

00:00:02.347 --> 00:00:08.732
Adding fourteen days to a discharge timestamp creates a follow-up point two weeks later.

00:00:08.732 --> 00:00:11.817
Adding thirty days creates a longer window.

00:00:11.817 --> 00:00:16.107
The interval makes the rule explicit and readable in PostgreSQL.

00:00:16.107 --> 00:00:19.222
Choose temporal types based on meaning.

00:00:19.222 --> 00:00:24.162
DATE is for calendar dates without time of day.

00:00:24.162 --> 00:00:28.202
TIMESTAMP stores a date and time without a time-zone interpretation.

00:00:28.202 --> 00:00:35.212
TIMESTAMPTZ represents an instant in time and is usually safer for events that cross regions or

00:00:35.212 --> 00:00:37.040
daylight-saving changes.
